    {
      "id": "eDSNYDXz7RbKTCRPHKKVT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -650,
      "y": 6369.202406860459,
      "width": 1500.40478515625,
      "height": 247.5,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roundness": null,
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 642841419,
      "version": 9,
      "versionNonce": 1581525777,
      "index": "b0SB8",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789532412290,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 22,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "Why 3 levels?   root (trust anchor, offline)  ->  intermediate (does the signing)  ->  leaf (the server cert)\n- If intermediate_ca.key leaks: make a new intermediate from the root, re-issue leafs. Browsers keep trusting the same root.\n- If root_ca.key leaks: everything must be redone and the root re-imported in every browser / VM. So keep it offline.\n- Browser / VM only need root_ca.crt. The ALB sends leaf + intermediate (that is what chain.pem in ACM is for).\n\nNotes\n- --no-password --insecure  = private key not encrypted. Fine for a lab, ACM needs it unencrypted anyway.\n- Renew: before 1 year, re-run step 4 and re-import into ACM (ACM does not renew imported certs).\n- step-ca server, provisioners, ACME, auto-renew, systemd = advanced, NOT needed for this lab.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why 3 levels?   root (trust anchor, offline)  ->  intermediate (does the signing)  ->  leaf (the server cert)\n- If intermediate_ca.key leaks: make a new intermediate from the root, re-issue leafs. Browsers keep trusting the same root.\n- If root_ca.key leaks: everything must be redone and the root re-imported in every browser / VM. So keep it offline.\n- Browser / VM only need root_ca.crt. The ALB sends leaf + intermediate (that is what chain.pem in ACM is for).\n\nNotes\n- --no-password --insecure  = private key not encrypted. Fine for a lab, ACM needs it unencrypted anyway.\n- Renew: before 1 year, re-run step 4 and re-import into ACM (ACM does not renew imported certs).\n- step-ca server, provisioners, ACME, auto-renew, systemd = advanced, NOT needed for this lab.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
